// tests/fixtures/err_mid_fn_returns_arena_value.ubl
// A @tier(mid) function declares List<int> as its return type, but the
// value actually returned from inside `with arena(...)` is an
// ArenaRef<List<int>> — tagged, scoped to that block, gone the moment the
// function returns. The caller has no way to know that.
//
// This is rejected today, but via the ordinary TypeMismatch check
// (declared List<int> vs. actual &arena List<int>), NOT via tier_check's
// dedicated MidReturnContainsArenaRef rule. That rule checks the
// function's *declared* return type for an ArenaRef marker — but there is
// no surface syntax for writing "ArenaRef" in a type annotation at all,
// so as currently implemented MidReturnContainsArenaRef can never
// actually fire; TypeMismatch is what's doing the real enforcement here.
// See docs/MEMORY_MODEL.md.
//
// Expected: sema FAIL (TypeMismatch).

@tier(mid)
fn make_list() List<int> {
    with arena(64KB) {
        return [1, 2, 3]
    }
}

fn main() void {
    let x = make_list()
}
